Approach (Reversal Algorithm)
We rotate the array to the right by k steps using reversal.
First, normalize k using k = k % n to handle large values.
Reverse the first n - k elements.
Reverse the last k elements.
Finally, reverse the entire array.
This rearranges elements in-place to achieve the required rotation.

Complexity
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
